# secrets + generated state + data lake: never in history (the journal is data/, not git)
data/*
!data/nav_attestation.jsonl
!data/decision_ledger.json
!data/cashcarry_config.json
# DEEPSEEK'S OWN OUTPUT, allowlisted 2026-09-03. The flywheel's donate step is
# `git add -- data/ docs/research/`, and `git add` on an ignored path is a SILENT NO-OP -- so the
# second brain ran daily, committed, pushed, and published none of its own findings, while the
# commits it made ("independent cold-phase findings") carried other organs' files swept up by the
# same blanket add. Findings now also go to data/intelligence/deepseek/ (already allowlisted, and
# the tree the candidate compiler globs); these two are the AUDIT trail behind them -- what was
# claimed, and the seal proving it was written before any other agent's conclusion was read.
!data/deepseek_evidence.jsonl
!data/deepseek_seals/
# The universe map is the documented routing target for EVERY digger's data-source finds
# (R0311): box-local it is invisible to review and dies on reclone, which silently discards
# every seat's universe-map contribution. It is institutional memory, same class as the
# intelligence ledgers below.
!data/data_universe_map.json
# R0311's sibling: the RU seat's era-corpus shortlist is §33 evidence + cross-run resume
# state (mined_to_reply_depth), not generated state — untracked it dies with the box.
!data/btcsec_trading_topics.json
!data/ppomppu_kr_rail_corpus.json
!data/kr_venue_bank_rail.json
# KR s4 (2026-08-19): §33 evidence + the card-#35 blocking measurement. The notice archive is
# the PRIMARY record the collector never pulled (category=trade only); untracked it dies with
# the box and the enumeration becomes unverifiable.
!data/kr_bank_rail_transitions.json
!data/upbit_notice_announcements.jsonl
# The authority declaration is POLICY, not generated state: it says which component
# may reach which surface. It must be reviewable in a diff, because a grant that
# widens silently is the failure libs/ops/agent_authority.py exists to prevent.
!data/agent_authority.json
# The GPT-seat intelligence LEDGERS are institutional memory, not generated state: they record
# what was fetched, at what completeness, and what remains unread. Ungitted they die with the
# container, and the next session re-reads a corpus it has already paid for.
# Only the INPUT ledgers: external_intel.json is the generated report and stays out.
!data/intelligence/
!data/intelligence/video_channel_coverage.json
!data/intelligence/extreme_return_claims.json
!data/intelligence/practitioner_corpus.json
# Stage-A screen results are EVIDENCE named in ledger rows (R0288 cites this path), not generated
# state: a gitignored evidence path is a dangling citation on every machine but the one that ran it,
# and §33 requires a named artifact to exist and be non-empty. 12K.
!data/unlock_event_screen.json
# The immutable-core seal is EVIDENCE, not state: it must travel with the code it protects, or a
# fresh clone has nothing to compare the constitution against and the fence degrades to a no-op.
# Its diff is also the audit trail -- a changed hash in a commit names exactly which law moved.
!data/constitution_core.lock
# The Gate 0 sign-off is EVIDENCE of a principal decision, not state: the live
# guard on the VPS reads it, so it must travel with the repo or the gate never
# sees it. Revocation = delete the file and commit that too.
!data/gate0_signoff.json
# REPO-scope max_audit acks are DISPOSITIONS OF A COMMITTED FACT, not runtime state (R0393). A
# REPO defect is identically true in every checkout, so an ack living only in the untracked
# registry left it firing on the VPS -- where the doctrine's own ">48h un-acked ESCALATES to the
# principal page" rule pages him for a defect that already carries a full reasoned disposition in
# another checkout. That is the exact failure the ack mechanism exists to prevent, and it fires
# hardest on the most carefully dispositioned items. RUNTIME acks stay untracked and per-box,
# where their truth genuinely differs by machine.
!data/max_audit_acks_repo.json
# The L1.45 excitation design is the PRE-REGISTERED HYPOTHESIS, not state. An uncommitted
# pre-registration is not a pre-registration: arms/epsilon/cap could be edited after seeing the
# fills with no trace, which is the exact confounding the design exists to remove. Its diff IS
# the audit trail -- a changed arm in a commit says a NEW experiment started, on that date.
!data/excitation_design.json
# The execution re-entry conditions are L1.16a EVIDENCE: the named enabling change, the dated
# probe window and the falsifier for every symbol on the execution denylist. Untracked, a symbol
# could be quietly re-admitted with no record of what change justified it.
!data/execution_reentry.json
# THE GUARD BLOCKS WHEN THIS FILE IS ABSENT, which is the correct direction and exactly why it
# cannot be untracked: data/* is ignored wholesale, so on a fresh clone or a wiped data/ the
# conviction sleeve would refuse EVERY entry and read as a quiet market. Committed so its absence
# is impossible rather than merely unlikely, and so a revised FOMC date is a reviewable diff
# (the Fed's dates are tentative until the preceding meeting confirms them). R0276.
!data/event_calendar.json
# A HIGH-WATER MARK STORED WHERE `rm` RESETS IT IS NOT A FLOOR. data/* is ignored wholesale, so
# the capability ratchet -- which exists precisely so no aspect can silently fall -- would have
# had its own history live only on whichever box last ran it. That is the failure mode the
# coverage ratchet already avoids by living in docs/ (see the note further down), and the
# reason the constitution ratchet requires a hand-edited dated file to weaken. Committed so a
# regression has to survive review rather than a lost file.
!data/CAPABILITY_RATCHET.json
# THE BASELINE IS THE MEASUREMENT. probe_bybit_archive answers "is the free 345-day Bybit L2
# archive expiring?" by comparing today's earliest-available date to the one it recorded LAST
# time. Untracked, a fresh clone or a wiped data/ has no prior, every run reports BASELINE, and
# the rolling-retention alarm the file exists to raise can never fire -- a detector that cannot
# fire is the class L0070 is named for. The seeded BTCUSDT prior carries its own provenance.
!data/bybit_archive_retention.json
# JP miner 2026-08-12. Disposition evidence for the premium-index axis: how much information the
# SETTLED funding print destroys (41.6% of owned 8h windows sit on a censoring constant; 68.8% of
# the live 812-symbol cross-section sits on one of three). Tracked because the axis card cites it
# as the reason the tie-break is worth building, and an untracked citation is an unverifiable one.
!data/jp_funding_clamp_census.json
# JP miner 2026-08-12. The マケデコ (market-api) calendar ground map, 74 entries 2023-2025. Tracked
# for the same reason as the botter calendar: the coverage row claims this ground is MAPPED, and an
# untracked map makes that claim unverifiable and re-scannable by the next seat.
!data/jp_makedeco_advent_calendar.jsonl
# KR miner 2026-08-12. The Ppomppu 가상화폐 era corpus: a post-no -> date calibration of the whole
# 12-year board (site search is robots-FORBIDDEN, so this map is the ONLY legal seek index and
# rebuilding it costs a fresh binary search) plus the 2,130-row title tape and the threads mined to
# comment depth. Tracked because watchlist card kr_rail_state_transition_global_leg cites both paths
# as its §33 evidence and its primary sources -- untracked, the card cites something no other clone
# can see, which is the one thing §33 says did not happen.
!data/ppomppu_bitcoin_era_map.json
!data/ppomppu_kr_era_threads.jsonl

# R0313 delisted-instrument rosters. Tracked for exactly the reason the file above is: the names
# are IRREPLACEABLE the moment a venue ages one off its own dead list. BitMEX carries 3077 settled
# contracts against 32 live ones, and nothing obliges it to serve them forever -- an untracked
# roster wiped with data/ cannot be re-fetched, only re-lost. The registry rides along so a clone
# can tell "this venue publishes nothing" from "this venue was never asked".
!data/delisted_instruments.json
!data/delisted_rosters/
!data/delisted_rosters/*.json
web/*
!web/index.html
!web/zentech.html
reports/
lake/
docs/EXTERNAL_PANEL_DOSSIER.md
# commit-audit payload: 425KB of `git log --since=24h` patches, REGENERATED on every run by
# ops/run_commit_audit.sh. Same class as EXTERNAL_PANEL_DOSSIER.md above -- a derived panel
# payload, not an artifact. Committing it would add a ~425KB blob per run for zero information
# (every byte is reconstructable from git itself), and §36 governance rightly applies to what is
# COMMITTED, so the PRODUCER carries the cadence claim instead (ops/crontab.manifest).
docs/research/recent_changes.md
*.exe
tools/*.exe

# Coverage reports are MEASUREMENTS, not records. The ratcheted high-water marks live in
# docs/research/COVERAGE_RATCHET.json and are committed; the raw report is regenerated on every
# run and would otherwise churn a large file on every commit.
coverage.json
mt5cov.json
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Test-planted probes. `test_the_dead_caller_check_can_still_SEE_a_dead_caller` writes these into
# the tree and removes them in a `finally`, but a `git add -A` landing inside that window commits
# them -- which happened on 2026-08-08 and shipped two junk files to the branch. The test itself
# ASSERTS they are absent when it starts, so a leaked pair turns the suite red on the next run.
# Ignoring them makes the race harmless without weakening the test.
libs/_deadlink_probe.py
scripts/_deadlink_probe_caller.py

# Positive-control probe planted and removed by tests/scripts/test_wiring_and_ratchets.py. It was
# committed once by a `git add -A` that ran while the test held it on disk, and a committed probe
# FAILS that test on every fresh clone (it asserts the probe is absent before planting one). The
# ignore makes that race unrepeatable.
libs/_orphan_probe_do_not_import.py
# one-shot gate-optimality diagnostic scratch (6MB pickle + root-level probes)
_audit_prepared.pkl
docs/audit_shards/

# per-box role (primary|research) -- R0107: never committed, each box declares its own
ops/role

# STRAY-CWD ARTIFACTS. libs/ops/fresh.py and every organ write cwd-RELATIVE paths BY DESIGN --
# see the _root() docstring: guessing an install root was itself a bug of this module's class,
# and all 151 cron lines pin `cd "$QUANT_ROOT"`. So a data/ tree under scripts/ can only be
# litter from something invoked with the wrong cwd (observed 2026-08-05 from a test run:
# scripts/data/freshness_contracts.jsonl + .fresh_markers/). It is ignored rather than
# committed because committing one would make a phantom SECOND freshness ledger permanent --
# exactly the two-sources-of-truth failure fresh.py exists to close.
# NARROW ON PURPOSE: libs/data/ is real source (28 tracked files) and tests/data/ holds
# fixtures, so a `**/data/` rule would hide both.
/scripts/data/

# PRINCIPAL DROP -- NEVER COMMIT. data/inbox holds material the principal supplies by hand from
# CLOSED sources: private WeChat groups, Telegram channels, paid substacks, login-walled pages.
# `data/*` above already covers it; this entry is explicit and separate because the failure here
# is IRREVERSIBLE -- publishing a private group's contents to a git remote cannot be undone by a
# later commit, and a future `!data/<something>` exception added in good faith for an artifact
# could otherwise widen the hole silently. The scored OUTPUT (reports/principal_drop.json) is
# ignored too: it quotes up to 600 characters of the source material verbatim.
data/inbox/
data/inbox/**
reports/principal_drop.json

# AGENT WORKTREE SCRATCH -- and this one is not tidiness, it is the deploy path.
# `git worktree add .claude/worktrees/<name>` leaves a directory containing a `.git` FILE, which
# `git add -A` (scripts/git_snapshot.py:25) records as a GITLINK (mode 160000) even though this
# repo has no .gitmodules and these are not submodules. A gitlink's recorded sha changes the
# instant that worktree commits anything, so the parent tree reads ` M .claude/worktrees/<name>`
# permanently and CANNOT BE CLEANED: committing the gitlink only re-points it, and the next
# worktree commit re-dirties it. deploy/pull_deploy.sh refused on any tracked dirt, so this
# turned the box's only inbound deploy path into a permanent no-op (measured 2026-08-12:
# 0 deploys in 1078 ticks). Four gitlinks were untracked the same day.
.claude/worktrees/

# one-off operator scripts; scratch/ is ruff-excluded in pyproject
/check_*.py
/chk_*.py
/dbg_*.py
/debug_*.py
/fix_*.py
/patch_*.py
/show_*.py
/test_*.py

# Per-box daily-cycle stamp. MUST NOT be shared between machines: it records "the operating chain
# already ran for this UTC day", and only the Windows box with a live MT5 terminal can actually run
# the shadow step. Committing a stamp written on a research box would make the execution box pull
# it, see the day as done, and skip the one run that matters.
desks/mt5/data/daily_cycle_state.json

# CREDENTIALS. Never tracked. secrets/ was NOT ignored until 2026-08-17 -- a FRED API key
# landed there and `git check-ignore` returned no match, meaning one `git add -A` would have
# committed it. Any key that has been in this directory on an unignored commit is burned.
secrets/

# Generated research artifacts under the desk data dirs. The code that produces
# them is committed and they are reproducible from it; an 18 MB parquet cache in
# git history is a mistake that cannot be taken back.
desks/*/data/**/*.parquet
desks/*/data/hunt_candidates.json
desks/*/data/recover_candidates.json

# Runtime state files (mt5-state branch only)
**/shadow_health.json
**/gateway_state.json
**/sleeves.json
**/regime_state.json
**/sync_marker.jsonbackups/

# BIS speech corpus: a 123MB source archive GitHub rejects; the DERIVED
# cb_tone_series.jsonl is the committed artifact, the zip is re-downloadable
# from https://www.bis.org/speeches/speeches.zip in one request.
desks/mt5/data/intelligence/central_banks/bis_speeches/

# FX Blue RAW harvest waves: ~14MB per 350-account wave and re-harvestable in ~40min
# from a public keyless route. The committed artifact is mechanism_digest.jsonl.gz.
desks/mt5/data/intelligence/fxblue/track_records*.jsonl

# Regime-fit memo. Purely a cache: every entry is keyed on the bar it was fitted on and is
# reproducible by refitting, so committing it would push an hourly-churning blob through the
# box's sync for no recoverable information. The STATE VECTOR itself (state_vector.json) is a
# record of what the desk believed at a moment and stays tracked.
desks/mt5/data/state_fits.json

# `reports/` above is ignored because reports are measurements. STATE_ADMISSION.json is not a
# measurement, it is a DECISION: `pf_allocator._live_state` reads it and withdraws a state
# dimension's access to the posterior when that dimension is in the graveyard. A `!` negation
# cannot reach inside an excluded directory, so the file is force-added once and tracked
# thereafter -- git reports changes to a tracked file regardless of these rules, which is exactly
# the behaviour wanted: the box's re-judged verdicts travel back with its hourly sync.

# Discovery-loop caches (2026-09-04): fetched public READMEs, content-addressed feature blocks
# and the typed research memory are rebuilt by their engines; none is a decision record.
desks/mt5/data/repo_cache/
desks/mt5/data/features/
desks/mt5/data/memory/
desks/mt5/data/deep_forest_seen.json
